{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game","id":543529,"title":"Beasts in Werewolf game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-06T23:34:43-07:00","id":543529,"title":"Beasts in Werewolf game","content":"A topic for crossover setting issues for Begotten and Uratha, not stated on the page 312 of <b>Beast: The Primordial</b> preview. If you need more story seeds or develop a bit more crossover mythology for your game, here is great place to do this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here are mine thoughst that should be stated in crossover section:<br /> <br /> 1. Idigams <b>should</b> be pointed as First Fears, or related mostly to the Beasts Souls. Both look like main drive for humanity to make civilization in attempts to protect itself from they harm. Both are wild and untame. Maybe even part of Idigams <i><b>become </b></i>Beasts Souls to linger on the Earth?<br /> <br /> 2. Beasts should equate <i><b>Luna</b></i> with Dark Mother. Luna is known as Mother of Werewolves, is personification of Shapeshifting, Night and Madness - very suitable to Dark Mother figure. At least one of their mythological representatives is connected to the Moon also - the Greeks Hekate. And the rumors that Idigams are first children of Luna makes sense as her as Mother of Monsters.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Mage</b> section is better than <b>Werewolf</b> section in the way as it makes advice on what exactly Paths correnspond best with Beasts. I would very like to see Families pointed to Uratha in this way - the &quot;werewolf-like&quot; Beasts should be Anakim, Eshmaki or Ulgallu? What of the Nightmares best represent the fear of Uratha in your eyes and why?<br /> <br /> If you got any more setting ideas that would ease the crossover, write them here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-07-2015, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T23:40:46-07:00","id":543576,"title":"","content":"I figure any crossover involving Werewolves and Beasts talking about their mythos with each other will lead to the assumption that Luna is the Dark Mother. With Uratha being children she birthed in the Shadow with Father Wolf.<br /> <br /> Although it somewhat fits when they talk about Father Wolf being a child of the Dark Mother that went into the Shadow to find his own path. That it ended with him finding the suitable way to end his tale via his own Children fits with his Bane being the tooth and claws of those capable of taking up his mantle fits in the ability to dictate your own narrative and how it plays out. Hell, even plays into how Spirits all over the world STILL fear Father Wolf and his children despite vast swaths of them not even existing while he was roaming around.<br /> <br /> Hah, so many interesting ways this can play out. Glad WoD finally has a crossover friendly game that supplements or adds to other splats without taking away from their own awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":717,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","user":"Monghani","date":". 06-07-2015, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T23:54:29-07:00","id":543578,"title":"","content":"One of the names for the Dark Mother is Gaia, so instead equating the Dark Mother with Luna, I'd make Luna and the Dark Mother family, so instead of werewolves being little brothers, they're cousins.<br /> <br /> As for werewolf and beast crossovers, I'd mention that the easiest hungers to get along with werewolves would be punishment or prey. Hosts, claimed, spirits, pure and balehounds, all make excellent prey, and well spirits should stay on their side of the gauntlet is a rule that spirits love to break.<br /> <br /> As for Luna as the Dark Mother, I mean sure I could see it as an in character theory, as the truth, not so much. First of all, Luna is a spirit, not a goetia, so why are beasts most closely connected to the wrong spirit world? Luna is the goddess of madness and shapeshifting, not fear or hunger, and if the goddess of shapeshifting is their mother I'd expect beasts to be better at shapeshifting, I'd also expect them to be better at driving people mad too.<br /> <br /> Also, if war against the pure is any indication, all of Luna's children are vulnerable to silver (even her children by adoption, since all shapeshifters are vulnerable to silver, no matter what their origin is), and if Luna sends her lunes to communicate with werewolves and not beasts? That would imply that the dark mother likes werewolves better than beasts, especially with her being a spirit and not a goetic being anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 06-07-2015, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T00:29:59-07:00","id":543589,"title":"","content":"I'd like to remind people that in 2nd ed the genders of Mother Wolf &amp; Luna aren't consistent amongst the Uratha. Either may be the Dark Mother or her descendants.<br /> <br /> On a lighter note, I really want to play a game with a Begotten packmate; Totem merit included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T00:52:07-07:00","id":543599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game?p=543578#post543578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the names for the Dark Mother is Gaia, so instead equating the Dark Mother with Luna, I'd make Luna and the Dark Mother family, so instead of werewolves being little brothers, they're cousins.</div> </div> </div> </div>This come to me few minutes ago. Yes, if Gaea is Dark Mother, then Uratha are cousins to Beasts. Still, if Gaea is Mother of Monsters - what does this say about World of Darkness as planet Earth? Think about it - spirit of the planet is the greatest monster of them all, with unsateable Hunger, wanting to devour her children. <i><b>Terrifying</b></i>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-07-2015, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T01:32:37-07:00","id":543622,"title":"","content":"Why not both? There's most likely Astral versions of Luna and Gaia close to the power level of their Spirit counterparts, given how often moon and earth goddesses show up in myths and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T06:46:47-07:00","id":543854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game?p=543599#post543599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This come to me few minutes ago. Yes, if Gaea is Dark Mother, then Uratha are cousins to Beasts. Still, if Gaea is Mother of Monsters - what does this say about World of Darkness as planet Earth? Think about it - spirit of the planet is the greatest monster of them all, with unsateable Hunger, wanting to devour her children. <i><b>Terrifying</b></i>...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, a nasty thought isn't it? It reminds me of Scion, in which Gaia is a titan that actively hates humanity.<br /> <br /> To give the notion a little bit of credence, isn't the axis mundi or some other realm in the astral plane called the soul of the world? It's been a while since I cracked open my copy of the astral book. And some beasts believe the Dark Mother is the primordial dream itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T08:11:34-07:00","id":543905,"title":"","content":"Is Gaea still a level 10 spirit in Werewolf? I know she was supposed to be in 1e, whereas Luna and Sol were Rank 8 or so... Or did that change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T08:29:12-07:00","id":543909,"title":"","content":"Ranks 8, 9 and 10 were mostly question marks and &quot;here be celestines&quot; signs. Gaea was speculated to either be 9 or 10, and Luna and Sol were 8 or 9. The new book doesn't even make a guess.<br /> <br /> I'd hesitate to put <i>anything </i>at 10 though. It's the top of the pile, Capital-G-God territory.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T08:34:01-07:00","id":543914,"title":"","content":"Imperial Mysteries kinda pegs Gaia as Rank 9, and Luna and Helios as Rank 8. But that's a Mage supplement, and first edition besides.<br /> <br /> They mention in the Tokyo section of the Beast book that at least two Beasts have joined a werewolf pack full time, so I made those two and shoved them in the same pack. One is a shrine-guarding oni Anakim, and the other is a bloody Eshmaki raised by the Strix (sorry, Tengu as they're called in Japan) who quite commonly guard such structures themselves. Really, shrines are a big common point between Strix, Beasts, and Werewolves in Tokyo. They're a great way to gather such strange forces together under one roof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T08:41:19-07:00","id":543916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game?p=543854#post543854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, a nasty thought isn't it? It reminds me of Scion, in which Gaia is a titan that actively hates humanity.<br /> <br /> To give the notion a little bit of credence, isn't the axis mundi or some other realm in the astral plane called the soul of the world? It's been a while since I cracked open my copy of the astral book. And some beasts believe the Dark Mother is the primordial dream itself</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct, though it's not called Axis Mundi. I'm not more versed on the Astral right now than you are probably, but essentially, the order of operations is Individual Souls, Collecive Human Soul, World Soul. The Primordial Dream sits between the Collective Soul and the World Soul.<br /> <br /> We're kind of screwed, yeah","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T09:17:18-07:00","id":543941,"title":"","content":"Anima Mundi is what you are looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:11:13-07:00","id":544041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game?p=543916#post543916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are correct, though it's not called Axis Mundi. I'm not more versed on the Astral right now than you are probably, but essentially, the order of operations is Individual Souls, Collecive Human Soul, World Soul. The Primordial Dream sits between the Collective Soul and the World Soul.</div> </div> </div> </div> Considering that the path through the onerios, tenemos, and anima mundi is unique to the Awakened, I would question how much of the stuff from that division remains from an outside perspective. And how much of the stuff we remember from the 1e Astral remains, truth be told. The Supernal and Abyss seems to have divorced itself from the Astral, where in 1e the former was basically the fourth level of the Astral, and the latter a gaping hole between 3 and 4. I don't think we can clearly say that the Primordial Dream fits into the mage view of the Astral, anymore than we can say that CtL's dream walking does.<br /> <br /> Anyways, back on the idea of Gaia being the Dark Mother... most Mother of Monster myths (Tiamat, Nyx, Ceto and Echidna, Leviathan) have direct ties to oceans instead of solid ground, and a sea-dragon theme. Mother Earth tends to be more about the land over the sea or sky, and no a dragon theme. Gaia has a very solid feel to her, while the Dark Mother feels more Primordial Chaos-y. My knee jerk reaction is to start looking at the Dark Mother as an Idigam that was never captured on the moon, who gave birth to not only Mother Wolf, but the Spinner Hag and Plague Rat King.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-07-2015, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:14:39-07:00","id":544049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game?p=544041#post544041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Considering that the path through the onerios, tenemos, and anima mundi is unique to the Awakened, I would question how much of the stuff from that division remains from an outside perspective. And how much of the stuff we remember from the 1e Astral remains, truth be told. The Supernal and Abyss seems to have divorced itself from the Astral, where in 1e the former was basically the fourth level of the Astral, and the latter a gaping hole between 3 and 4. I don't think we can clearly say that the Primordial Dream fits into the mage view of the Astral, anymore than we can say that CtL's dream walking does.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's openly stated in Beast where it is according the Mage cosmology. It's, like, the first thing you read about the Primordial Dream. Page 73-74.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-07-2015, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:16:02-07:00","id":544051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game?p=544049#post544049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's openly stated in Beast where it is according the Mage cosmology. It's, like, the first thing you read about the Primordial Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's unusual. Huh. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:28:56-07:00","id":544065,"title":"","content":"It's where they appear <i>to a mage</i>. A beast can tunnel straight from there to any bit of the astral they like, so location is kind of a fuzzy concept as far as they're concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T14:24:50-07:00","id":544289,"title":"","content":"Werewolf territories are probably breeding grounds for Heroes, what with Lunacy causing Integrity loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:10:41-07:00","id":544406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game?p=544289#post544289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf territories are probably breeding grounds for Heroes, what with Lunacy causing Integrity loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if they go by the Oath and kill witnesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:13:30-07:00","id":544411,"title":"","content":"They don't need to do that. The witnesses usually forget anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T18:00:59-07:00","id":544586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game?p=544411#post544411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't need to do that. The witnesses usually forget anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitively not always. It is even encouraged as something Pure to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T18:12:35-07:00","id":544601,"title":"","content":"I don't know about that, the Pure seem to have an 'open secret' going on in some of their breeding grounds. It may have been kept over in second edition, since the Ivory Claws in Holmes County seem to have an arrangement with the people there, as well as many human allies.<br /> <br /> But if a human has lost integrity via Lunacy, they've also forgotten or at least rationalized what's happened. And while the book suggests you don't use just Integrity loss via witnessing the supernatural as a source of Heroes, it also causes outbursts of violence through Atavism, a constant retreat or catatonic state through Delusion, or predation or possession via spirits through Reception. I like the Reception one, though I never got a response on how it 'feels,' and if someone's afflicted with the Condition and gets a Dramatic Failure, they just disappear into the Hisil. Which must be scary.<br /> <br /> Though they couldn't be affected by Lunacy, I suppose a Wolf-Blooded could become a Hero as well. And since they'd keep their Wolf-Blooded tell, would a Wolf-Blooded with a Shadow Twin who turned into a Hero also have their twin turn into one? And what kind of spirits would pop up around a Hero? Fear, of course, but surely some other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T18:18:14-07:00","id":544631,"title":"","content":"Re: Luna as the Dark Mother -- it <i>is</i> worth noting that in astrology, Lilith is an alternate name for the &quot;dark moon&quot; of a person's natal chart. *waggles eyebrows and leaves*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T22:05:23-07:00","id":544794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game?p=544631#post544631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Luna as the Dark Mother -- it <i>is</i> worth noting that in astrology, Lilith is an alternate name for the &quot;dark moon&quot; of a person's natal chart. *waggles eyebrows and leaves*</div> </div> </div> </div> I was about to ask about that. Goetia reflect not what is, but what people think, so Luna as mother of monsters only works if people think of moon deities as mother of monsters.<br /> <br /> Even werewolves see Luna less as a mother of monster and more mother of shapeshifters, which beasts aren't that adept at. <br /> <br /> And of course there's the fact that Luna as goetia formed from human opinion would logically be younger than Luna as actual moon goddess, which would make beasts less than primordial and more johnny come latlies. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T05:12:30-07:00","id":545028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game?p=544631#post544631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Luna as the Dark Mother -- it <i>is</i> worth noting that in astrology, Lilith is an alternate name for the &quot;dark moon&quot; of a person's natal chart. *waggles eyebrows and leaves*</div> </div> </div> </div> Good point. The moon is also tied to the idigam (primordial monsters) and affects the ocean and sky, two of the major families in the game. I am really liking Luna = Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game?p=544794#post544794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was about to ask about that. Goetia reflect not what is, but what people think, so Luna as mother of monsters only works if people think of moon deities as mother of monsters.<br /> <br /> Even werewolves see Luna less as a mother of monster and more mother of shapeshifters, which beasts aren't that adept at.<br /> <br /> And of course there's the fact that Luna as goetia formed from human opinion would logically be younger than Luna as actual moon goddess, which would make beasts less than primordial and more johnny come latlies.</div> </div> </div> </div> What does goetia have to do with this? *Slow blink* I assume you're talking about Mage goetic magic, and not real life...<br /> <br /> And shapeshifters are a kind of monster, so wouldn't that be the same thing as Luna as a mother of monsters? I have seen stories where the Moon was tied to the fae and vampires as well - not WoD stories, but it is part of pop culture...<br /> <br /> Also, aren't Atavisms basically shapeshifting? Well, at least in part? You turn part of your body into your spiritual reflection - its a lot like Uratha turning Garou by that reasoning, no?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game?p=544065#post544065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's where they appear <i>to a mage</i>. A beast can tunnel straight from there to any bit of the astral they like, so location is kind of a fuzzy concept as far as they're concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div> I just got the kickstarter preview, and looked it up. It does seem that Beasts see it between those layers too, not mages (it seems more debatable if mages even know the Primordial Chaos exists, though haven't read that much...).<br /> <br /> Though, all this is a bit odd, because their Souls are outside of their Oneiros. I don't quite get it yet. I'll have to read more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-08-2015, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T09:03:34-07:00","id":545371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game?p=545028#post545028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does goetia have to do with this? *Slow blink* I assume you're talking about Mage goetic magic, and not real life...</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/terra-incognita-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">Per 2e Mage</a>, &quot;goetia&quot; is the term for Astral entities as a whole rather than just your inner demons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, aren't Atavisms basically shapeshifting? Well, at least in part? You turn part of your body into your spiritual reflection - its a lot like Uratha turning Garou by that reasoning, no? </div> </div> </div>Nope.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p16</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 <b>Beasts physically transform into monsters:</b> Mostly false. <u>Beasts do not shapeshift in the traditional sense</u>, though they can use powers called Atavisms to temporarily gain certain advantages related to their Souls\u2019 true shapes.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though, all this is a bit odd, because their Souls are outside of their Oneiros. </div> </div> </div>It's not quite as simple as that.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p74</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>A Beast\u2019s Lair is similar to a human\u2019s Oneiros</u>, with the Soul as its guardian. Its dreamscape reflects her history, personality, and evolving nature.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p120</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>The Soul itself never leaves the Lair</u> (barring Inheritance; see p. XX) <u>and no power can force it to do so</u>, as the Lair is just as much part of the Beast\u2019s Soul as the Primordial Self within it.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-08-2015, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:11:04-07:00","id":546124,"title":"","content":"After some thinking and looking back over Werewolf, I've started thinking more and more about the Luna / Helios separation. They're opposites - Helios suppresses the Hisil, and sends the essence flowing out of the Hisil into the Material, while Luna reverses it, bringing the Shadow to life, reviving spirits, etc. I actually don't see any mention of Gaia the earth as a spirit at all in 2e. Even the rankings for spirits tops out with Celestial, it seems, from reading the book. <br /> <br /> And, I have a little pet theory, from Requiem. The CotC revere the Dark Mother, who is very likely the same as the Beast's Mother. The L+S are all about the angels, (And thus, God-Machine!). VII has rumors of angels, and the Ordo spit in God's face. We have a large Dark Mother v. God duality here in vampire.<br /> <br /> Changeling preview of Tokyo from the Beast have hinted that the freehold are calling themselves Moon Princesses. Or something like.<br /> <br /> So, I've started a new World of Darkness cosmological theorycraft! On the one hand, champion humans and humanity, we have the God-Machine, the Sun, the Light! On the other, we have the Dark Mother, the Moon Maiden, Luna! Its a nice duality that flows well between the four games we have out for 2e so far. I'm going to run with it!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:24:05-07:00","id":546146,"title":"","content":"It's only mentioned once in second edition, and very little in first, but in Werewolf it's spelled Gaea, as in Pangaea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:05:10-07:00","id":546560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/543529-beasts-in-werewolf-game?p=543909#post543909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ranks 8, 9 and 10 were mostly question marks and &quot;here be celestines&quot; signs. Gaea was speculated to either be 9 or 10, and Luna and Sol were 8 or 9. The new book doesn't even make a guess.<br /> <br /> I'd hesitate to put <i>anything </i>at 10 though. It's the top of the pile, Capital-G-God territory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An early mage book declared the primal wild as a rank 10 entity, but that has never been mentioned again, so I presume that's fallen by the wayside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}